  "id": "COMPOUND:29842 - PROTEIN:6149",
  "verbalization": "Taiwanin C is implicated in the interaction with High-affinity choline transporter through a series of molecular pathways, with Caspase-5 acting as a central mediator. The evidence suggests that Taiwanin C targets Caspase-5, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including (2R,3S,4R,5R,6S)-2-[...]-oxane-3,4,5-triol and 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[...]-phenol. All these compounds are linked to the High-affinity choline transporter, indicating a potential mechanism where Taiwanin C may influence the activity of this transporter through Caspase-5. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Caspase-5 and ultimately on the choline transporter suggests a possible role in modulating choline transport, possibly through proteolytic or signaling mechanisms. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Caspase-5 in linking Taiwanin C to the choline transporter, offering a plausible mechanism for the observed interaction.",
